The 'cuts' option of TMVA is used to tune \(D^{0}\) cuts. This option randomly sample different cut sets in the variable space, calculate signal and background efficiency for each cut set. Then one cut set with lowest background efficiency at certain signal efficiency. We can then pick the cut set with the best significance according to the signal and background yield corresponding to the whole data set of 1.3 B events. Fig. 3.19 shows the lowest background efficiency, significance and so on vs. signal efficiency for \(p_{T}\) between 2 and 3 GeV/\(c\). We can see that as cuts get tighter, signal and background efficiency both decrease, but background efficiency decreases much faster. The best significance for 1.3 B events is around signal efficiency of 10%. However, because the

